  "text": "A language model has to finish this sentence. [curious] So... which word comes next? First, it gives every candidate a score, called a logit. Say cat scores three point two... and rock scores minus zero point four. Then softmax turns those scores into probabilities. It raises e to each score, and divides by the total. Cat gets sixty-five percent... and rock gets under two.\n\nTemperature divides every score, before the softmax. The order never changes... only the shape does. Below one, the gaps between the scores grow. At zero point two, cat takes over ninety-nine percent! And at zero, it always takes the top token. That's greedy decoding. Above one, the gaps shrink, and the bars even out. At one point five, rock rises to almost five percent.\n\nNow let's draw twenty tokens at each setting, from the same twenty random numbers. At zero point two? All twenty come out cat. At one point five, cat wins only eleven. Dog, bird... and even rock get a turn.\n\nTop p adds a guard. Keep the likeliest tokens until they cover ninety percent... and drop the rest. At one point five, that keeps cat, dog and bird. Rock is cut before the draw.\n\nSo turn temperature DOWN when there's one right answer, like extraction or code. And turn it UP when you want variety.",
